# 📌 Project Overview

The **Day Ahead Electricity Price Forecasting Platform** is an end-to-end machine learning application developed for forecasting hourly electricity prices across European electricity markets.

The project combines:

- Energy market analytics
- Feature engineering
- Machine learning forecasting
- Forecast validation
- Explainable AI
- Interactive Streamlit dashboard

The objective is to simulate a real-world forecasting workflow supporting:

- Energy Analysts
- Electricity Traders
- Portfolio Managers
- Risk Analysts
- Market Intelligence Teams

---

# ⚠️ Demo Repository Notice

This repository contains the **demo deployment version** of the project.

The complete local implementation contains additional resources including:

- Historical market datasets
- Intermediate processed datasets
- Trained machine learning models
- Forecast artifacts
- Extended evaluation outputs
- Production forecasting pipelines

These files are intentionally excluded from GitHub due to repository size limitations and deployment constraints.

The GitHub version includes:

- Complete source code
- Interactive Streamlit dashboard
- Forecasting workflow
- Demo datasets
- Model evaluation framework
- Feature engineering pipeline

The demo reproduces the functionality of the forecasting platform while using representative sample datasets for deployment.

# 🎯 Business Problem

Electricity prices in European energy markets are highly volatile due to:

- Demand fluctuations
- Renewable generation variability
- Fuel prices
- Conventional generation availability
- Market conditions


Accurate day-ahead price forecasting is essential for:

- Energy trading
- Portfolio optimization
- Risk management
- Renewable integration
- Market analysis


The objective of this project is to predict hourly electricity prices using historical market and generation data.


